/capita): Below-average municipal income dampens discretionary beverage spending and consumption volume.", "Off-Peak Seasonal Dampening: Non-summer months (especially Winter and late Autumn) naturally reflect ~15-20% lower national beverage consumption and fewer recycling trips."], "actionable_suggestions": ["External Parking Plaza Placement: Position the RVM in the external customer parking lot near the main access road rather than in a rear store aisle. This allows car-based commuters and bulk depositors to drop 50-100 bottle bags directly from their car trunk without entering the store aisles.", "Dedicated RVM Signage & External Directional Wayfinding: Install prominent directional signage at the store entrance and customer parking lot directing shoppers directly to the Coripet recycling point. Clear visibility increases spontaneous bottle deposits by +15% to +25%.", "Institutional Community Partnerships: Connect with local schools, municipal sports centers, and environmental clubs. Designating this machine as the official collection node for school recycling competitions drives consistent, high-volume youth and family participation.", "Proactive Staff Emptying Protocol: Train store personnel to empty collection bags promptly when the 80% bin-full alert is triggered. In high-volume stores, machine-full downtime on busy Friday/Saturday afternoons permanently destroys up to 25% of potential daily volume."], "accuracy_variance_factors": ["Tourist / Commuter Corridor Effect (Potential Under-Prediction): The model\'s baseline uses permanent municipal census data (18468 inh in Marche). If this store sits on a regional tourist gateway (e.g. alpine ski/hiking routes, coastal vacation corridors, or state highways), seasonal floating foot traffic can swell actual collection volumes by +30% to +80% above permanent census projections.", "Mechanical Bin Capacity & Servicing Bottlenecks: For stores with demand exceeding ~750 bottles/day, bin capacity fills rapidly. If store personnel fail to empty collection bags promptly, machine full-bin downtime will artificially depress actual collected volume below theoretical demand.", "Geocoding Centroid Fallback: The location was resolved at municipal centroid (\'STREET_LEVEL_DATABASE_MATCH\'). Exact street-level walking catchment may exhibit slight variance in local commercial foot traffic."], "collection_rate_drivers": ["Substantial Commercial Scale: Store footprint (2576 m2 sales area, 16 checkouts) generates strong continuous shopper throughput capable of sustaining above-average recycling volumes.", "Sufficient Population Base: Municipal population (18,468 inhabitants) provides adequate local customer volume for sustainable operation.", "Undiluted Local Network Buffer: Zero competing Coripet machines within 3 km (3.7 km to nearest node) grants this machine an exclusive, insulated local collection zone.", "Restricted Disposable Income (EUR 14,469 PIL/capita): Below-average municipal income dampens discretionary beverage spending and consumption volume.", "Off-Peak Seasonal Dampening: Non-summer months (especially Winter and late Autumn) naturally reflect ~15-20% lower national beverage consumption and fewer recycling trips."]}, "lifecycle_horizon": {"launch_month_num": 10, "launch_month_name": "October", "launch_year": 2026, "rampup_enabled": true, "macro_annual_growth_rate": 0.055, "year1_rolling_profile": [{"lifecycle_month": 1, "lifecycle_label": "M01 (Oct \'26)", "calendar_month_num": 10, "calendar_month_name": "October", "calendar_year": 2026, "days_in_month": 31, "maturity_factor": 0.65, "maturity_pct": "65%", "daily_bottiglie": 997.6, "daily_presenze": 37.8, "monthly_target_bottiglie": 30926, "seasonal_context": "Autumn steady-state", "lifecycle_stage": "Onboarding & Discovery (Ramp-up M1)", "is_rampup": true, "post_ramp_month": null}, {"lifecycle_month": 2, "lifecycle_label": "M02 (Nov \'26)", "calendar_month_num": 11, "calendar_month_name": "November", "calendar_year": 2026, "days_in